  "slug": "dark-energy-constraining-early-6aff",
  "summary": "Five preprints probe the DESI-motivated dark energy behavior via scalar potentials, axion-like models, early dark energy tails, and averaged inhomogeneous cosmologies.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is testing what physical structure could underlie a DESI-motivated evolving dark energy signal and related scalar-field phenomenology. One preprint reconstructs two-field canonical-phantom potentials reproducing a phantom-divide transition. Another confronts a generalised axion-like quintessence model with CMB, BAO, supernova, SH0ES, chronometer and GRB data against LambdaCDM. The early dark energy work argues that the post-peak damping tail carries information on the scalar potential beyond peak parameters. A separate preprint asks whether DESI's redshift dependence can instead arise from dark-energy-free averaged dust cosmologies. The chameleon paper is adjacent: it gives exact n=1 multilayer solutions and forecasts CANNEX Casimir-force constraints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
